{"id":"n534a067978","headline":"The Dollar Has Followed in the Yen’s Footsteps","summary":"The US dollar fell to its lowest level since May after the Treasury raised its long-term bond buybacks from $2 billion to $4 billion. The move followed a yen-linked decline in the dollar.","why":"The US Treasury's debt buyback operations affect long-term yields and market liquidity. The dollar's level influences global capital flows, commodity prices and emerging-market currencies.","category":"markets","event_type":"rates","importance":3,"flag":null,"market_moving":true,"location":{"place":"New York","country":"United States of America","lat":40.713,"lon":-74.006,"region":"na"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"ActionForex","url":"https://www.actionforex.com/contributors/fundamental-analysis/651277-the-dollar-has-followed-in-the-yens-footsteps/"},"sources":[{"name":"ActionForex","url":"https://www.actionforex.com/contributors/fundamental-analysis/651277-the-dollar-has-followed-in-the-yens-footsteps/"}],"published_at":"2026-08-20T09:57:03Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T00:21:16Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"c4c7ae116cefc6f0","impacts":[],"why_moved":"The Treasury increased its long-term bond buybacks from $2 billion to $4 billion, and the dollar then fell to its lowest level since May.","backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T00:21:16Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-08-20T09:57:03Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-08-20T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"JA","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/banknotes-money-1963184.jpg","alt":"banknotes money (illustration)","credit":"stevepb","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/money-laundering-crime-fighting-196